From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: don't fail the removal of a station

mac80211 doesn't allow a sta_state callback to fail for a down transition,
but ath11k_mac_op_sta_state() passes on the result of the peer delete. With
crashed firmware that is -ESHUTDOWN, which on a deauthentication before a
restart trips the check in mac80211:

  wlan0: failed to remove key (0, xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx) from hardware (-108)
  WARNING: net/mac80211/sta_info.c:1603 at __sta_info_destroy_part2+0x144/0x168
  Call trace:
   __sta_info_destroy_part2+0x144/0x168 (P)
   __sta_info_flush+0x154/0x220
   ieee80211_set_disassoc+0x4cc/0x664
   ieee80211_mgd_deauth+0x13c/0x5fc

The failure doesn't matter here: mac80211 goes on either way, the code
below the call drops a peer entry that the delete left behind, and the
firmware has no peers once it restarts. On WCN6855 the early vdev stop can
fail first, and ath11k_mac_station_remove() then returns before its cleanup,
so the station stays counted and its stats stay allocated, as they did
before this patch. Warn in the log as before and report success.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index ef3fb5069..cb51b3da1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10022,6 +10022,9 @@ static int ath11k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		mutex_unlock(&ar->ab->tbl_mtx_lock);
 
 		ath11k_cfr_decrement_peer_count(ar, arsta);
+
+		/* mac80211 doesn't allow a down transition to fail. */
+		ret = 0;
 	} else if (old_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTH &&
 		   new_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC &&
 		   (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP ||
